Package: warsi
Architecture: any
Depends: appstream,
         dconf-gsettings-backend | gsettings-backend,
         flatpak,
         libbge0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: glycin-loaders,
            packagekit
Description: BlankOn Linux app store: Flatpak apps, system updates, .deb files
 Warsi is BlankOn Linux's app store, built with GTK4 and libadwaita. It lets
 you discover, install, update and remove Flatpak apps, browse curated and
 Flathub content, and manage add-ons.
 .
 It also shows pending APT system package updates on the Library page and
 installs them through PackageKit, either on the next restart (offline
 update) or immediately, and notifies about app and system updates.
 .
 Opening a downloaded .deb file shows Warsi's package installer, which
 lists what else it installs or removes and installs it through
 PackageKit. Warsi is the default application for .deb files in GNOME.
 .
 Install packagekit for the system updates and the .deb installer.
 .
 Warsi is based on Bazaar (https://usebazaar.org), patched by
 BlankOn Linux. It has its own app ID (id.blankonlinux.warsi) and can be
 installed next to Bazaar.

Package: libbge0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Library to make GTK Extensions for Bazaar
 Bazaar GTK Extensions (bge) is a small library of GTK4 widgets used by
 Bazaar, the Flatpak app store, such as an animation framework, a carousel
 and a Markdown renderer.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

